<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hēmĭcyclium</span></b> ,
			ĭi, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμικύκλιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a half-circle</i>, <i>semicircle</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Vitr.
				9, 8, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 5, 6,
			33</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A semicircular recess</i>, <i>with
				seats</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Lael. 1, 2</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 2,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A semicircular public place furnished with rows of
				seats for learned discussions</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Gramm. 17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>A semicircular kind of sundial</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 9, 8,
				1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
